WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.487
Let’s walk through Simulation Settings.

00:00:02.487 --> 00:00:05.575
Treat move, phase, and timer controls as room-level

00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:06.888
state changes.

00:00:06.888 --> 00:00:10.012
Confirm operator intent before acting, make one change at

00:00:10.012 --> 00:00:13.525
a time, and verify the shared tracker immediately afterward

00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:13.650
.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.800
On this slide, advance or reverse moves and phases

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.050
, start or pause the timer, and reset the

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:19.938
clock.

00:00:19.938 --> 00:00:23.125
In practice, treat every control as a room-level state

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:24.062
change.

00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:27.887
Confirm intent before acting and verify the tracker afterward.

00:00:28.385 --> 00:00:31.560
When you are ready, use Open Simulation Settings to

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.523
move to the live surface.

00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:36.285
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:36.435
.
